{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The guarantees "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes about overlapping, cancelled, and reset calls."}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/concurrencyandcancellation"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Modeling state","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatePreviewError","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Pagination"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Modeling-state"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and built under Swift 6 strict concurrency. Every "},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadNextPage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call is "},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which raises three questions the moment a screen does more than one of them: what happens if a second call starts before the first finishes? How do you stop one early? And how do you force a store back to a known state outside of any of them? This article covers all three."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Overlapping calls only ever apply the latest result","level":2,"anchor":"Overlapping-calls-only-ever-apply-the-latest-result"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing extra is needed to handle a screen firing off a second call before an earlier one has finished — a fast double-tap on Retry, or a new search query arriving before the previous one resolved:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["await store.load { try await api.fetchArticle(id: 1) } \/\/ slow — still in flight","await store.load { try await api.fetchArticle(id: 2) } \/\/ fast — resolves first"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Internally, every call stamps itself with a token before running "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and only applies its result — "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or the "},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" mapping "},{"code":"loadCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" do — if that token is still the most recently started one by the time "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" resolves. In the example above, article 1’s slower fetch resolving "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}]},{"type":"text","text":" article 2’s result is already showing never overwrites it; its result is silently dropped. "},{"code":"refresh(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" follows the same rule: it only clears once the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"newest"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in-flight refresh finishes, not whichever overlapping one happens to resolve first. "},{"code":"loadNextPage(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"isLoadingNextPage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" follows it too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need to call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for this to hold — it’s automatic. Reach for "},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when you additionally want to stop the older call’s work from running at all, not just prevent its result from landing."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancelling explicitly","level":2,"anchor":"Cancelling-explicitly"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to stop whatever call is currently running, without waiting for it to resolve:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["store.cancel() \/\/ e.g. from onDisappear, or right before firing off a newer query"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (and "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are left exactly as they were — cancelling never surfaces a "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the way letting "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself fail would. This applies uniformly, including to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadWithRetry(maxAttempts:backoff:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" cancelled mid-backoff: it stops retrying and leaves "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" untouched, just like every other call. If nothing is in flight, "},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does nothing."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Cancelling automatically","level":2,"anchor":"Cancelling-automatically"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A store also cancels whatever it was still tracking when it’s deallocated, as a last-resort safety net — you don’t need to call "},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" yourself. In practice this rarely has anything to do: "},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/etc. already "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" their own work to completion before returning, so by the time a store can actually be deallocated, there’s normally nothing left in flight to cancel. It exists to guard against that assumption changing later, for free."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Resetting outside of a load","level":2,"anchor":"Resetting-outside-of-a-load"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/reset(to:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" snaps a store back to "},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (or any state you give it) without going through "},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at all — useful for a full sign-out flow, where whatever the store was showing or fetching no longer applies to the next signed-in user:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func signOut() {","    session.clear()","    articlesStore.reset() \/\/ back to .loading, as if freshly created","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like "},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", it stops whatever operation is currently in flight; unlike "},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", it also immediately replaces "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and clears "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so a screen bound to the store reflects the reset right away instead of waiting for a cancelled operation to unwind."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"Concurrency & Cancellation","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/loadWithRetry(maxAttempts:backoff:_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", but retries a failing ","type":"text"},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"settling into ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after the first failure. ","type":"text"},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" stays","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" across every attempt; only the final failure (once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxAttempts","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is reached) or a success changes it.","type":"text"}],"title":"loadWithRetry(maxAttempts:backoff:_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadWithRetry(maxAttempts:backoff:_:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/loadwithretry(maxattempts:backoff:_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"loadWithRetry","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxAttempts","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"backoff","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Duration","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8DurationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"@Sendable","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" () ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateStoreC5Valuexmfp","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/reset(to:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Snaps the store back to ","type":"text"},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by default), outside of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call — useful for a full sign-out\/reset flow,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"where whatever the store was showing or fetching no longer applies.","type":"text"}],"title":"reset(to:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/reset(to:)","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatestore\/reset(to:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reset"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"to"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ScreenState","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A5StateO"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Value","preciseIdentifier":"s:12ScreenStates0A10StateStoreC5Valuexmfp"},{"kind":"text","text":">)"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","title":"ScreenState","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore":{"title":"ScreenStateStore","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "